<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54667" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατα-νύσσω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stab, gouge</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ὀφθαλμούς τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phleg.
					36.4J.
				</span></i>
			:—elsewh. in 
				Pass.
			, with fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νῠγήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Si.</u>
					20.21
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ενύγην</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span> (v. infr.); <i>to be
				sorely pricked</i>, metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατενύγησαν τὴν καρδίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					2.37
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				34.7
			</span></i>: hence, <i>to be bewildered, stunned</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάθισον -νενυγμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Is.</u>
					47.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ps.</u>
				4.5
			</span></i>, al.; <i>keep silence</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Le.</u>
				10.3
			</span></i>.</div>
